The '''Sarafone national football team''' ({{Lang-bw|Kooṣo Sarafoneed}}) represents [[Sarafone]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Sarafone Football Federation]] and competes as a member of the North and Central Kaftia Football Association within the [[AFA]] confederation.

Sarafone are currently ranked 55th in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]] and qualified for their first-ever [[AFA World Cup]] at the [[2022 AFA World Cup|2022 tournament]].

== History ==

=== Development ===
Sarafone's football history is closely tied to the broader Burawi-speaking world. The Sarafone Premier League was established in 1998, later than many neighbours, but the country's athletic tradition produced a generation of physically imposing players who have drawn interest from clubs across Kaftia and the Mesogean.

=== First World Cup ===
Sarafone's qualification for the 2022 World Cup was considered a surprise, as the team defeated more established Kaftian sides in the qualifying playoffs. The squad is built around a defensive core and rapid counter-attacking football.

